{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_event_stream_eventstream", "label": "EventStream", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/event-stream.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A system-wide bus for one-to-many messaging that does not fit the parent-child or sender-receiver shape: the publisher does not know how many subscribers exist and the subscribers do not know who publishes."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_event_stream_eventkey", "label": "EventKey", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/event-stream.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gives a plain kind-tagged type the call shape a class gets for free, and carries the event type so a predicate sees the real shape. The bare string is the shorthand and costs the typing plus typo protection."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_event_stream_classchannel", "label": "Class channels (instanceof matching)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/event-stream.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Subclass instances reach base-class subscribers, which makes hierarchical event taxonomies easy \u2014 subscribers pick their level."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_event_stream_kindchannel", "label": "Kind channels", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/event-stream.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A kind channel matches exactly one kind \u2014 kinds have no base, so there is no way to say \"every billing.* event\". A class and a kind are two channels even when the class instances carry that kind, so holding both means two deliveries per publish."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_event_stream_predicatefiltering", "label": "Predicate filtering", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/event-stream.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Filtering on the bus side is cheaper than inside every subscriber. Predicate-bearing subscriptions do not dedup because predicate functions have no identity contract, a throwing predicate counts as no-match, and predicates run at publish time on the publisher stack."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_event_stream_builtinevents", "label": "Built-in event types", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/event-stream.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Everything the framework publishes is a class, so class channels remain the way to reach them; kind channels are for application events. CurrentClusterState is deliberately not on the bus \u2014 it states where one subscriber is starting from, which is not news to anybody else."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_event_stream_eventstreammisuse", "label": "When not to use the event stream", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/fundamentals/event-stream.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "For exactly one receiver, hold the ref \u2014 the bus is for fan-out and using it to avoid typing a ref adds cost and obscures intent. It is a coordination tool, not a data pipeline."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_event_stream_eventstream", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_fundamentals_actor_system_actorsystem", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confiden